  "testbench": {
    "name": "comparator-regeneration",
    "description": "Decision time versus input overdrive over PVT at 50 mV / 1 mV / 0.1 mV, the regeneration time constant tau extracted from the two small rungs, the near-metastable behaviour at 0.1 mV, and the switching energy and static current per decision.",
    "claim": "PLACEHOLDER DUT. sim/dut.json binds sim/dut/placeholder_comparator.spice (id placeholder-v1, provenance placeholder). This record substantiates the harness -- that a three-overdrive transient regeneration sweep genuinely runs and tau is genuinely extracted from it over the full PVT grid -- and is NOT evidence toward README.md#target-specification's Decision-time-vs-overdrive row until design/comparator.sch exists and sim/dut.json is repointed at it (spec/porting-plan.md next step 1).",
    "experiment": "comparator-regeneration",
    "directory": "testbench",
    "netlist": "tb_regeneration.spice",
    "netlist_sha256": "e7877bd74198947dbc12a3441847792865af72cac26487e60f4f76f18a777315",
    "manifest_sha256": "8baa13593ad7d9ba4e7b0b180909f4d6ff7321bca25a91c998df3ac69b91627c",
    "nominal_supply_v": 1.2,
    "supply_tolerance": 0.1
  },
  "checks": {
    "td_od50_ns": {
      "min": 0.001,
      "max": 25.0,
      "min_spread_pct_by_axis": {
        "process": 1.5,
        "temperature": 8.0
      },
      "description": "PRIMARY CORNER-SENSITIVITY ANCHOR as well as the row-facing number. The min/max pair is a sanity envelope, not the spec bound: 1 ps would mean the delay measurement latched onto a numerical artefact, and 25 ns is most of the strobe window. The SPEC bound (README.md's decision-time row) is deliberately NOT encoded while sim/dut.json binds a placeholder. The per-axis floors are what make --sabotage-corners fail: regeneration speed is set by device transconductance, which is corner- and temperature-sensitive. Floors calibrated from this experiment's first committed 45-point record (named in this experiment's README.md, run --no-write during issue #8 development), with ~40% margin below the observed weakest slices (process 2.61%, temperature 12.76%). The supply axis is unfloored because the delay threshold is supply-normalized on purpose (see the deck header), which removes most of the supply dependence from the measurement by construction (observed weakest supply slice: 2.02%)."
    },
    "tau_ps": {
      "min": 0.1,
      "max": 20000.0,
      "description": "Regeneration time constant, extracted from the (1 mV, 0.1 mV) pair -- both inside the logarithmic region, one decade apart, so tau = (t(0.1 mV) - t(1 mV))/ln(10). Bounds are a sanity envelope: a negative or sub-0.1 ps tau means the two delays came out in the wrong order, and 20 ns means the structure is not regenerating on the timescale of the strobe."
    },
    "resolve_decades": {
      "min": 1.0,
      "description": "How many e-folds of regeneration fit inside the measured 1 mV decision time (td_od1 / tau). It is the metastability lever arm: the probability of an unresolved decision falls as exp(-t/tau), so this is the exponent that number is taken to."
    },
    "dout_od50_end": {
      "min": 0.9,
      "description": "POLARITY CHECK: after the second strobe the 50 mV instance must hold the POSITIVE answer (dout normalized to its own supply). Together with dout_od50_first below it proves the same instance decided BOTH ways within one run."
    },
    "dout_od1_end": {
      "min": 0.9,
      "description": "the same at 1 mV overdrive."
    },
    "dout_od01_end": {
      "min": 0.9,
      "description": "the same at 0.1 mV overdrive -- i.e. the near-metastable rung still resolves to the CORRECT answer within the strobe window, which is the statement the metastability row rests on."
    },
    "dout_od50_first": {
      "max": 0.1,
      "description": "the OPPOSITE-polarity half of the same proof: at the first strobe the input was negative, so the held output must be low."
    },
    "dout_od1_first": {
      "max": 0.1,
      "description": "the same at 1 mV overdrive."
    },
    "dout_od01_first": {
      "max": 0.1,
      "description": "the same at 0.1 mV overdrive."
    },
    "i_static_ua": {
      "min": 0.1,
      "description": "Static supply current of one instance with the strobe low. A floor only: zero would mean the bias never came up and every dynamic number in this record was taken on a dead circuit."
    }
  },
